IMPORT prelude

-- Layout-Designs of Integrated Circuits Act 1999 (Singapore) -- who is a qualified person and a qualified owner (s 2), what is
-- protected and for how long (ss 5, 6, 7), what infringes and what does not (ss 8 to 11, 23, 24), groundless threats (s 17),
-- assignments and licences (s 18), and the Government's duty to tell the owner (s 25).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/LDICA1999.txt. The edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021 (wef 01/04/2022), in ss 14, 15, 16 and 21.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0083 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a chip designer, a chip importer or reseller, or someone threatened
-- with proceedings would meet. Not encoded: the remedies themselves (s 12 damages, additional damages, ss 13, 14 delivery up and
-- disposal) beyond comments, the evidential presumptions (ss 15, 16), prospective ownership (s 19), exclusive licensees and
-- concurrent actions (ss 20, 21, 22), Government remuneration (s 26), the anti-competitive-practice licence (ss 27 to 29) beyond
-- its effect on infringement, rules (s 30) and the designation power (s 31) beyond its effect on "qualifying country". s 3 (no
-- protection for ideas) is a comment only. No designation notification under s 31 was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Layout-Designs of Integrated Circuits Act 1999 -- protection and infringement`

§§ `2 -- qualifying country, qualified person, qualified owner`

-- s 2(1) "qualifying country" means "(a) a country or territory, other than Singapore, which is a member of the World Trade
-- Organisation; or (b) a country or territory designated by the Minister under section 31".
DECLARE Country HAS
    `is Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of the World Trade Organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is designated by the Minister under section 31` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the country` IS A Country
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the country is a qualifying country` IF
        ((NOT `the country`'s `is Singapore`) AND `the country`'s `is a member of the World Trade Organisation`)
    OR  `the country`'s `is designated by the Minister under section 31`

-- "qualified person" means (a) a natural person (i) "who is a national of, or is domiciled or ordinarily resident in Singapore
-- or in a qualifying country", or (ii) "who has a real and effective industrial or commercial establishment for the creation of
-- layout-designs or for the production of integrated circuits in Singapore or in a qualifying country"; or (b) a person other
-- than a natural person (i) incorporated or formed in Singapore or a qualifying country, or (ii) with such an establishment
-- there; "and includes the Government and the government of a qualifying country".
-- Below, "a covered country" means Singapore or a qualifying country.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a national of, domiciled or ordinarily resident in a covered country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is incorporated or formed in a covered country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a real and effective design or chip-making establishment in a covered country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the Government or the government of a qualifying country` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is a qualified person` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is the Government or the government of a qualifying country`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `has a real and effective design or chip-making establishment in a covered country`
    OR  (`the claimant`'s `is a natural person` AND `the claimant`'s `is a national of, domiciled or ordinarily resident in a covered country`)
    OR  ((NOT `the claimant`'s `is a natural person`) AND `the claimant`'s `is incorporated or formed in a covered country`)

-- "qualified owner" means (a) a qualified person who, under s 6(1), is the owner; or (b) a person who, under s 6(1), is the owner
-- of a layout-design "which was not commercially exploited anywhere else in the world before it was commercially exploited in
-- Singapore or in a qualifying country"; "and includes a person, whether or not a qualified person, who is a successor in title
-- to a qualified owner". s 6(2): a qualified person can be a qualified owner even if sharing ownership with one who is not.
-- INFERENCE: limb (b) is read as needing a first commercial exploitation in Singapore or a qualifying country; a design never
-- exploited anywhere is taken not to satisfy it.
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `owns it under section 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `first exploited in a covered country` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a successor in title to a qualified owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is a qualified owner` IF
        `is a successor in title to a qualified owner`
    OR  (`owns it under section 6(1)` AND (`the claimant is a qualified person` `the claimant` OR `first exploited in a covered country`))

§§ `6 -- who owns a layout-design`

-- s 6(1): "Subject to any agreement to the contrary": (a) not commissioned and not in the course of employment -- the creator;
-- (b) "created pursuant to a commission -- the person who commissioned the layout-design is the owner"; (c) "not created
-- pursuant to a commission but is created by an employee in the course of his or her employment -- the employer is the owner".
-- s 2: for a computer-aided design, the "creator" is "the person who made the arrangements for the creation".
-- A commission beats employment: a design made by a contractor's employee under a commission belongs to the commissioner.
DECLARE Owner IS ONE OF
    `the creator`
    `the person who commissioned it`
    `the employer`
    `whoever the agreement names`

GIVEN `pursuant to a commission` IS A BOOLEAN, `by an employee in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `an agreement provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Owner
`the owner of the layout-design` MEANS
    IF `an agreement provides otherwise` THEN `whoever the agreement names`
    ELSE IF `pursuant to a commission` THEN `the person who commissioned it`
         ELSE IF `by an employee in the course of employment` THEN `the employer`
              ELSE `the creator`

§§ `5, 7 -- protection and its duration`

-- s 3: the Act "does not apply in relation to any idea, procedure, process, system, method of operation, concept, principle or
-- discovery". (Not encoded beyond this comment.)
-- s 5(1): the Act protects a layout-design "owned by a qualified owner" that is "original in the sense that it is the result of
-- its creator's own intellectual effort and is not commonplace" (or a commonplace combination that is original taken as a
-- whole). (2) independently created identical designs are each protected. (3) no protection for a design "created before
-- 15 February 1999". (4) a design "is deemed not to have been created until it has been recorded in documentary form or
-- incorporated into an integrated circuit, whichever is earlier". No registration step appears anywhere in the Act.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of` MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `year recorded in documentary form` IS A NUMBER, `year incorporated into a chip` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of creation` MEANS `the earlier of` `year recorded in documentary form` `year incorporated into a chip`

-- s 7: protection ends "(a) if it is first commercially exploited within 5 calendar years after the calendar year in which it
-- was created, at the end of the 10th calendar year after the calendar year in which it was first commercially exploited;
-- (b) in any other case, at the end of the period of 15 calendar years after the calendar year in which it was created".
-- s 24(2), s 28(2): an act under Government use (s 23) or a Court licence (s 27) "is not to be taken into account in calculating
-- the duration of protection". The year given below is the first exploitation NOT counting those acts.
-- INFERENCE: exploitation in the calendar year of creation itself is treated as "within 5 calendar years after" it.
-- Consequence: a design never exploited is protected for 15 years; one exploited in its year of creation, for only 10.
DECLARE Design HAS
    `owned by a qualified owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `original` IS A BOOLEAN
    `created on or after 15 February 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
    `year created` IS A NUMBER
    `commercially exploited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `year first commercially exploited` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the design` IS A Design
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last calendar year of protection` MEANS
    IF      `the design`'s `commercially exploited`
        AND `the design`'s `year first commercially exploited` AT MOST `the design`'s `year created` PLUS 5
    THEN `the design`'s `year first commercially exploited` PLUS 10
    ELSE `the design`'s `year created` PLUS 15

GIVEN `the design` IS A Design, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the design is protected in` IF
        `the design`'s `owned by a qualified owner`
    AND `the design`'s `original`
    AND `the design`'s `created on or after 15 February 1999`
    AND `the year` AT LEAST `the design`'s `year created`
    AND `the year` AT MOST `the last calendar year of protection` `the design`

§§ `8 to 11, 23, 24 -- infringement and the acts that are not`

-- s 8: the qualified owner may (a) copy, and authorise copying, "whether by incorporation into an integrated circuit or
-- otherwise"; (b) commercially exploit. s 2: "commercially exploit" includes to sell, hire or distribute by way of trade, to
-- offer or expose for sale, or "to import for the purpose of sale". s 9: doing either "without the consent of the qualified
-- owner" infringes. s 2(3), (4): acts and copies include a substantial part.
-- s 10, not an infringement: (a) copying a part that is not original; (b) copying "for a private purpose and not for the purpose
-- of commercial exploitation"; (c) copying "for the sole purpose of evaluation, analysis, research or teaching"; (d), (e) using
-- the results to create, and then copying or exploiting, a different original layout-design; (f) the owner of an identical,
-- independently created design acting on that other design; (g) commercially exploiting a copy, chip or article "after [it]
-- has been commercially exploited, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, by, or with the consent of, the qualified owner".
-- s 11(1): commercially exploiting an unauthorised copy, chip or article is not an infringement if, when the person acquired
-- it, the person "did not know, and could not be reasonably expected to have known" it was unauthorised; (2) once aware, the
-- shelter continues "if and only if the person pays to the qualified owner such remuneration" as agreed or set by the Court.
-- s 23(1): an act by the Government, or a person authorised in writing by it, "for a public non-commercial purpose" is not an
-- infringement; s 24(1)(d) it "does not permit the sale ... to the public". (s 24(1)(e), predominantly in Singapore, is not
-- modelled.) s 27: a Court licence to remedy an anti-competitive practice (its effect taken as consent; INFERENCE).
-- Note the asymmetry: (b) and (c) cover COPYING only, (g) and s 11 cover COMMERCIAL EXPLOITATION only.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `the layout-design is protected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `copies it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commercially exploits it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the qualified owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `copies only a part that is not original` IS A BOOLEAN
    `copies for a private purpose, not for commercial exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `copies solely for evaluation, analysis, research or teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts on a different original design made from that analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts on an identical design it independently created` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the item was already put on the market by or with the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired it not knowing and with no reason to know it was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has since become aware` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pays the remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is Government use for a public non-commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Government use involves sale to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts under a Court licence under section 27` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the innocent acquirer is sheltered` IF
        `the conduct`'s `acquired it not knowing and with no reason to know it was unauthorised`
    AND (   (NOT `the conduct`'s `has since become aware`)
         OR `the conduct`'s `pays the remuneration`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copying infringes` IF
        `the conduct`'s `copies it`
    AND NOT (    `the conduct`'s `copies only a part that is not original`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `copies for a private purpose, not for commercial exploitation`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `copies solely for evaluation, analysis, research or teaching`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `acts on a different original design made from that analysis`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `acts on an identical design it independently created`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exploitation infringes` IF
        `the conduct`'s `commercially exploits it`
    AND NOT (    `the conduct`'s `acts on a different original design made from that analysis`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `acts on an identical design it independently created`
             OR  `the conduct`'s `the item was already put on the market by or with the owner's consent`
             OR  `the innocent acquirer is sheltered` `the conduct`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government use defence applies` IF
        `the conduct`'s `is Government use for a public non-commercial purpose`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `the Government use involves sale to the public`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct infringes` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the layout-design is protected`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `has the qualified owner's consent`)
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `acts under a Court licence under section 27`)
    AND (NOT `the Government use defence applies` `the conduct`)
    AND (`the copying infringes` `the conduct` OR `the exploitation infringes` `the conduct`)

-- s 12(1): the owner has the remedies "available with respect to any other property rights"; (2) additional damages having
-- regard to "the flagrancy of the infringement". s 13(2): no delivery-up order unless a disposal order under s 14 is also made
-- or there are grounds for one. (Not encoded.)

§§ `17 -- groundless threats`

-- s 17(1): where a person "by means of circulars, advertisements or otherwise, threatens another person with proceedings" for
-- infringement, "whether or not the person making the threat is a qualified owner", the Court may on the application of a
-- person aggrieved declare the threat unjustified, grant an injunction, or award compensation. (2) not if the defendant shows
-- the acts "constituted, or would constitute, an infringement"; (3) "The mere notification of the existence of a right ... does
-- not constitute a threat"; (4) no application "where the threat is to bring a proceeding for an infringement that is alleged to
-- consist of making or importing anything"; (5) an advocate and solicitor acting for a client is not liable.
DECLARE Threat HAS
    `threatens infringement proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a mere notification that the right exists` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the alleged infringement is making or importing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the threatener shows the acts infringe` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made by an advocate and solicitor for a client` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the threat` IS A Threat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person aggrieved may get relief` IF
        `the threat`'s `threatens infringement proceedings`
    AND (NOT `the threat`'s `is a mere notification that the right exists`)
    AND (NOT `the threat`'s `the alleged infringement is making or importing`)
    AND (NOT `the threat`'s `the threatener shows the acts infringe`)
    AND (NOT `the threat`'s `is made by an advocate and solicitor for a client`)

§§ `18 -- assignments and licences`

-- s 18(1): a right in a layout-design "is movable property"; (2) assignment may be total or partial; (3) "An assignment is
-- ineffective unless it is in writing and signed by or on behalf of the assignor". (4) a licence by a qualified owner "binds
-- each successor in title ... except a purchaser in good faith for value without notice (actual or constructive) of the licence
-- and a person who derives title from the purchaser". s 2: an "exclusive licence" is "a licence in writing signed by or on
-- behalf of a qualified owner".
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by or on behalf of the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assignment is effective` IF `in writing` AND `signed by or on behalf of the assignor`

GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `for value` IS A BOOLEAN, `without notice of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `derives title from such a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence binds the successor` IF
    NOT (   (`in good faith` AND `for value` AND `without notice of the licence`)
         OR `derives title from such a purchaser`)

§§ `25 -- the Government must tell the owner`

-- s 25(1): after an act under s 23 the Government must inform the qualified owner -- (a) in "national emergency or other
-- circumstances of extreme urgency, as soon as reasonably practicable"; (b) otherwise "promptly". (3) nothing requires it to
-- inform or disclose "if doing so would or might reasonably be expected to prejudice the defence or security of Singapore".
-- s 26: the Government must also pay remuneration (agreed, by agreed method, or set by the Court). (Not encoded.)
DECLARE Deadline IS ONE OF
    `as soon as reasonably practicable`
    `promptly`
    `no duty to inform`

GIVEN `in a national emergency or extreme urgency` IS A BOOLEAN, `would prejudice defence or security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Deadline
`when the Government must inform the owner` MEANS
    IF `would prejudice defence or security` THEN `no duty to inform`
    ELSE IF `in a national emergency or extreme urgency` THEN `as soon as reasonably practicable`
         ELSE `promptly`
